From 7a077bd236fccfd21860ce2c301221839e8ff02a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Andrzejczak <mit.mis@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 00:13:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/51] begonia-wifi (fwport): stub
 linux/irqchip/mtk-gic-extend.h for vendor BTIF

Vendor mtk_btif.h pulls <linux/irqchip/mtk-gic-extend.h> for mt_irq_dump_status();
no mainline equivalent. Add a no-op inline stub in the compat include tree.

wmt_drv now compiles + links clean (LD wmt_drv.o); this unblocks the vendor BTIF.

Signed-off-by: Michal Andrzejczak <mit.mis@gmail.com>
---
 .../compat/include/linux/irqchip/mtk-gic-extend.h         | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/misc/mediatek/connectivity/compat/include/linux/irqchip/mtk-gic-extend.h

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/connectivity/compat/include/linux/irqchip/mtk-gic-extend.h b/drivers/misc/mediatek/connectivity/compat/include/linux/irqchip/mtk-gic-extend.h
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..b4c94118e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/connectivity/compat/include/linux/irqchip/mtk-gic-extend.h
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 */
+/* compat stub: linux/irqchip/mtk-gic-extend.h (begonia fwport).
+ * Vendor BTIF includes this only for mt_irq_dump_status(); no mainline
+ * equivalent. Provide a no-op so the IRQ-dump debug path compiles. */
+#ifndef _COMPAT_STUB_MTK_GIC_EXTEND_H
+#define _COMPAT_STUB_MTK_GIC_EXTEND_H
+static inline void mt_irq_dump_status(int irq) { (void)irq; }
+#endif
-- 
